# Defensive deny-list for a build done with the repository root as its context. None of the
# current images use it (their context is python-packages/liturgos-auditor-stt, which has its own
# allow-list .dockerignore), but a future `docker build .` from here must not send the git history,
# virtualenvs, secrets or voice data to the daemon or bake them into an image.
# Nested patterns start with **/ because a pattern without it only matches at the context root.

# Version control history and local agent/tooling state.
.git
.claude

# Python virtualenvs and caches: large, platform-specific, and not reproducible inside an image.
**/.venv*
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/.pytest_cache
**/*.egg-info

# Secrets: compose env files (AUDITOR_STT_API_KEY, CSV_ADMIN_TOKEN) and private keys.
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/*.pem
**/*.key

# Service and training state (job state, ledger, audio store, datasets, model downloads, runs,
# exports, registry). It holds voice recordings and models trained on them. These are the
# directories the CLI creates as ./data and ./models when run from a source checkout, and the
# ones the images mount as /data and /models. If the source ever gains a real package or folder
# named data or models, narrow these two patterns.
/data
/models
**/data
**/models
**/*.sqlite
**/*.sqlite3
**/*.sqlite-journal
**/*.sqlite-wal
**/*.sqlite-shm

# Recordings and video in the containers this project handles (the repository root holds a local
# test video, kept out of git by .gitignore). Voice data is personal data: see docs/data-protection.md.
**/*.mp4
**/*.mkv
**/*.mov
**/*.wav
**/*.ogg
**/*.oga
**/*.opus
**/*.webm
**/*.m4a
**/*.mp3
**/*.flac
**/*.aac

# Logs.
**/*.log
